{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3434","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3434","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3434\",\"parent_revision\":\"928fc8f2f30e1813488ae4d5752dcc2dc3264a0743e88c2126ab358ec67b5aeb\",\"root_revision\":\"928fc8f2f30e1813488ae4d5752dcc2dc3264a0743e88c2126ab358ec67b5aeb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nRuntime skill text names TeamCreate as a live tool an agent can call. The tool was removed.\\n\\nEVIDENCE\\n\\nhttps://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-teams (accessed 2026-09-06), page note: \\\"This page describes agent teams as of v2.1.178. With CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS set, spawning a teammate no longer needs a setup step ... Before v2.1.178, you asked Claude to create and name a team first, and Claude used the TeamCreate and TeamDelete tools to set it up and remove it. Both tools no longer exist. The team_name input on the Agent tool is accepted but ignored.\\\"\\n\\nThe same page's warning states agent teams are experimental and disabled by default, requiring CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1. So even the replacement mechanism is not available unless a consumer opts in.\\n\\nOCCURRENCES\\n\\nplugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md names TeamCreate in two places: the \\\"How to spawn agents\\\" list and the \\\"Quick Reference: Agent Delegation\\\" section. Both currently sit on main.\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nAn agent following the instruction calls a tool that does not exist, and the failure surfaces as a tool error rather than as guidance to use the current mechanism. Because the text also presents teams as the answer for \\\"agents need to communicate\\\", it steers agents toward an experimental, off-by-default feature instead of ordinary concurrent dispatch.\\n\\nA sweep should cover every runtime file naming TeamCreate or TeamDelete, not only the two known occurrences.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the same docs page describes the current mechanism (Claude launches a teammate by calling the Agent tool with a name while agent teams are enabled), which is what the replacement text should describe, with the availability condition stated.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Claim verification against Claude Code docs, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9f6593bb66fabe7d9659e1ac688cc5af4d46f4b00fda52b1080d5b46211f2a6d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSA7iQ\"}"}